\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee steady on SBI dlr sales,oil imports. \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2000\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, May 30 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was quoted little changed from the morning's levels in Tuesday afternoon trade with steady dollar supplies from the State Bank of India (SBI) preventing a slide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Constant dollar buying to meet import demand was still there and a state-run oil firm had also bought around $40-50 million, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 44.56/57 per dollar at 2:40 p.m. (0910 GMT). \par \par \uc2  It had opened at 44.49/51 before sliding on heavy dollar demand. \par \par \uc2  "The SBI has been there throughout...almost the entire market is buying from the SBI," a dealer with a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the SBI's continuous presence indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably did not want the rupee to weaken beyond current levels. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the rupee hit lows of 44.75 last week with a warning against speculation. \par \par \uc2  The RBI also imposed a 50 percent surcharge on the import finance rate and raised the interest on overdue export bills to 25 percent. \par \par \uc2  It said it will continue to sell dollars through the State Bank of India (SBI) and will meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs towards oil imports and some government debt payments. \par \par \uc2  The RBI said it was not considering monetary tightening immediately. But on Tuesday it placed on its open market sale list the 10.95 percent 2011 bond auctioned on Monday, which devolved heavily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It also placed several 364-day treasury bills on its sale list. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market may be wary of buying dollars above current levels after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves to absorb surplus liquidity from the market, but that had not resulted in any paying in the forward market. \par \par \uc2  "The forward to forward market has become somewhat illiquid. But there is a lot of receiving and stray paying in most maturities," a dealer with a state-run bank said. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium was quoted at an annualised 2.65 percent compared with Monday's 2.79. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5u04g95\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
