\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee shade lower on dlr bids at open. \b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2000\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, May 30 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly weaker in opening deals on Tuesday, slipping below the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  44.50 level, as banks built up dollar positions in anticipation \par \par \uc2  of import demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The rupee was quoted at 44.54/56 per dollar at 9:15 a.m. \par \par \uc2  (0345 GMT) after it opened at 44.49/51. \par \par \uc2      It ended Monday at 44.49/495, its weakest close ever. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market will however be wary of the State Bank \par \par \uc2  of India's (SBI) moves as the rupee extends losses, \par \par \uc2  after its dollar sales on Monday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  assurance last week it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when necessary through \par \par \uc2  the SBI. \par \par \uc2  "...unhedged import bids now putting pressure and \par \par \uc2  preventing rupee settling in a stable range. Till those bids \par \par \uc2  are out, a break of 44.50 is certain and a test of previous low \par \par \uc2  cannot be ruled out," Centurion Bank said in its market \par \par \uc2  commentary on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2       A spillover of cash imports after Monday's U.S. market \par \par \uc2  holiday was also likely. \par \par \uc2     Monday's rupee fall was largely on account of dollar \par \par \uc2  purchases by an aluminium firm towards an investment and \par \par \uc2  suspected demand towards foreign funds' outward remittances, \par \par \uc2  and the market was expecting that demand to continue, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Absence of sustained demand could trigger export sales, \par \par \uc2  especially after the SBI's dollar sales at levels over 44.50 on \par \par \uc2  Monday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Last week the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when \par \par \uc2  the rupee fell to its weakest level of 44.75, warning the \par \par \uc2  market against speculation. \par \par \uc2  The RBI on Thursday imposed a 50 percent surcharge on the \par \par \uc2  import finance rate and raised the interest on overdue export \par \par \uc2  bills to 25 percent. \par \par \uc2  It said it will continue to sell dollars through the State \par \par \uc2  Bank of India (SBI) and will meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  needs towards oil imports and some government debt payments. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward dollar premia will be soft, especially \par \par \uc2  in the near maturities since both the liquidity situation and \par \par \uc2  call rates were easy. \par \par \uc2  The RBI on Monday auctioned 11-year bonds worth 50 billion \par \par \uc2  rupees at which it set a cut-off yield of 10.95 percent. It \par \par \uc2  accepted subscriptions worth just 1.14 rupees and the issue \par \par \uc2  devolved to the extent of 48.86 billion on the RBI. \par \par \uc2  Call rates ended Monday easy at 6.9-7.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium ended at an annualised 2.79 percent \par \par \uc2  on Monday, compared with the previous day's 2.88 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708; \par \par \uc2  bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw5u04fl5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
