\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee to open weak, trade in wide range. \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2000\par 05:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BOMBAY, May 15 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par open slightly weak after Friday's close at lower levels,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * Market still uncertain about direction of the rupee and \par \par \uc2  tracking the State Bank of India's (SBI) moves keenly, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee's unexpected 0.85 percent fall to all-time lows \par \par \uc2  of 44.08 on Wednesday, and partial recovery on Thursday, were \par \par \uc2  both driven by the SBI, they said. \par \par \uc2      * The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both \par \par \uc2  days, but dealers believe the SBI was acting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may want a slightly weaker \par \par \uc2  trading band for the rupee, yet it will not be allowed to fall \par \par \uc2  beyond 44.0 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      * Friday's slide from highs of 43.85 was mostly inter-bank \par \par \uc2  driven and corporates stayed on the sidelines, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * Importers still not showing a keen interest to hedge, \par \par \uc2  hence lasting demand for dollars unlikely and the rupee will \par \par \uc2  soon settle into a range, they said. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended at 43.92/93 on Friday compared with the \par \par \uc2  previous day's 43.88/89. \par \par \uc2      * The benchmark Bombay stock index's fall to 11-month lows \par \par \uc2  on Friday also a cause for concern. \par \par \uc2      *  Forward premiums likely to be ranged as the market \par \par \uc2  awaits the result of the twin bond auction later in the day and \par \par \uc2  its impact on liquidity. \par \par \uc2      * The government announced the twin bond auction of 2003 \par \par \uc2  and 2006 maturity government bonds worth 50 billion rupees on \par \par \uc2  May 15 \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended at an annualised 2.42 percent \par \par \uc2  on Friday against 2.47 percent the previous day. \par \par \uc2       * India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $37.732 \par \par \uc2  billion on May 5, 2000 from $37.975 billion in the previous \par \par \uc2  week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly \par \par \uc2  statistical supplement on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  * Inflation, based on the wholesale prices, fell to 5.94 \par \par \uc2  percent in the week ended April 29 from 6.1 percent in the \par \par \uc2  previous week, the industry ministry said. \par \par \uc2  * Year-on-year M3 money supply growth fell to 15.8 percent \par \par \uc2  in the two weeks to April 21 from 15.9 percent in the preceding \par \par \uc2  two weeks, the RBI said.. \par \par \uc2  Previous closing rates: \par \par \uc2  Call money rates: 7.0-7.10 pct \par \par \uc2  BSE 30-share Index : 4,107.14 (-144.22) \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq Composite Index: 3,529.06 (+29.48) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Indust. Avg : 10,609.37 (+63.40) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Hang Seng Index\tab \tab    : 15,111.94 (+619.02)\par   Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab   : 17,357.86 (+475.40)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5f00m0o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100