\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee firms slightly vs dlr,trade cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2000\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, May 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was slightly firm in cautious trade on Friday morning as a jittery market tested lower levels for the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Opening quotes were seen around 43.85, but the market was still uncertain and light dollar bids emerged, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the scope for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firm much were limited and they expected dollar bids to be sustained. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.85/87 per dollar at 9:20 a.m. (0350 GMT) after it opened steady around Thursday's close at 43.88/89. \par \par \uc2  "I do not see the rupee appreciating beyond 43.83. There will be bids (for dollars) at that level," a dealer with a private bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the State Bank of India (SBI) was moving with the market in early deals and had not indicated strong buying or selling interest. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's unexpected 0.85 percent fall to all-time lows of 44.08 on Wednesday, and partial recovery on Thursday, were both driven by the SBI. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both days, but dealers believe the SBI was acting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf. \par \par \uc2  Early trade could be active as corporates put through cash-dollar transactions after Thursday's strike by bank employees to protest against the privatisation of banks affected trade in the cash market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market will be tracking the movement in the stock market. The benchmark Bombay stock index's fall to 10-month lows on Thursday was a cause for concern. \par \par \uc2  Corporate dollar demand to hedge imports is seen, since most of them were unhedged and Wednesday's move caught them by surprise, dealers said \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums are likely to be bid in the near term amid light import hedging of dollar exposures and liquidity concerns, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The government announced the twin bond auction of 2003 and 2006 maturity government bonds worth 50 billion rupees on May 15 \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium ended at an annualised 2.47 percent on Thursday against 2.4 percent the previous day. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000; fax 91-22-264 1708; vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5c00qwj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
