\par\par \b \uc2  Fitch-IBCA Executive Says India Reform Process Has Slowed  Down \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 06:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Bombay (Dow Joens)--Global investors are beginning to fear that India's reform process has slowed down, Pauk Rawkins, senior director of sovereign ratings at Fitch IBCA, said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Rawkins comments come ahead of an announcement by the ratings agency on India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating. The announcement is due Wednesday at 1100 GMT (7.00 a.m. EST). \par \par \uc2  "Investors feel that reforms have slowed down" and that is why India is missing out on foreign direct investment, he said. \par \par \uc2  Rawkins added that there is a "need to invigorate the reform process on the broad front." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He was speaking at the seminar on "Sovereign and Financial Sector Risk\par Assessment - India and Global Perspectives," organized jointly by Indian\par ratings agencies CARE and Fitch-IBCA.\par - - 08/03/00 06-12G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One of India's strengths is that its exchange rate is competitive\par vis-a-vis other Asian countries, said Rawkins. "The Reserve Bank of\par India has managed it (exchange rate) very well," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par India's exchange rate has been relatively free from sharp\par fluctuations, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  falling by 12% to 15% versus the dollar\par every year, largely thanks to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy followed by the\par Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also noted that the cost of bank restructuring as a percentage of\par the gross domestic product is lower in India than in many Asian\par countries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Recounting the strengths and weaknesses of the Indian economy, Rawkins\par said that India's strengths are the improved external debt position, and\par the unblemished external debt-service record.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He noted that for a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating, rating agencies look at\par the country's willingness and ability to pay. India, when faced with a\par balance of payments problem in 1991, indicated its ability to take tough\par decisions, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Also, he said, a matter of concern is India's low share in world\par trade, which discourages the flow of foreign direct investment into the\par country.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Other weaknesses of the country, relevant to the foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rating, are its huge fiscal deficit, high government debt, poor human\par capital and its narrow tax base.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The strengths include India's long record of established democratic\par institutions, and low cost labor.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Latha Venkatesh & Ramya Venugopal; 91-22-2884211;\par ramya.venugopal@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw38017w3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
