\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee seen in steady open, ranged trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 1999\par 05:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BOMBAY, Sept 1 (Reuters) - * Indian rupee\tab \tab expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to open steady and trade in a range amid a lack of fresh\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  factors or flows, dealers say. \par \par \uc2      * Exporter sales of dollars could continue but seem to be \par \par \uc2  normal remittances against bills, dealers say \par \par \uc2      * Customary dollar sales by banks on Wednesdays to take \par \par \uc2  advantage of weekend swap differences likely \par \par \uc2      * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping a watchful eye on the market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say dollar purchases by state-run banks seen this week \par \par \uc2  could be at the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) behest to prevent \par \par \uc2  rupee firming. \par \par \uc2  * The RBI last week said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  either directly \par \par \uc2  or through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  if the rupee \par \par \uc2  came under pressure and added it would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt \par \par \uc2  service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  * No major dollar supplies seen in the run up to elections \par \par \uc2  despite improved sentiment on the Bombay stock exchange which \par \par \uc2  closed at 4,898 points on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have turned buyers over the past few days \par \par \uc2  though they have been net sellers of over $50 million in Indian \par \par \uc2  markets in August after having invested nearly one billion \par \par \uc2  dollars in Indian markets in the April-July period. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended Tuesday at 43.48/485 per dollar against \par \par \uc2  Monday's close of 43.49/4925 \par \par \uc2      * Forward premiums seen ranged but market view mixed. \par \par \uc2      Some expect short-term inter-bank paying (sell-buy swaps) \par \par \uc2  on expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep liquidity tight to \par \par \uc2  ease pressure on the rupee until elections are over. \par \par \uc2      * Others feel there could be receiving to take advantage of \par \par \uc2  high US interest rates. \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended at an annualised 5.18 percent \par \par \uc2  against 5.25 percent on Monday. . \par \par \uc2      Closing rates on Tuesday: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates\tab \tab   : 9.75/10.0 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Pakistan rupee kerb closing   : 54.20/54.25\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bombay Stock index\tab \tab   : 4,898.21 (-7.68)\par     Dow Jones Indust. Avg\tab      : 10,829.28 (-84.85)\par     Hang Seng Index\tab \tab      : 13,482.77 (-205.89)\par     Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab     : 17,436.56 (-482.41)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9101g2p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
