\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee in a firmer range on exporter sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee firmed in afternoon trade on Tuesday on dollar sales by exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.465/4725 per dollar at 2:50 p.m. (0920 GMT), after opening steady at 43.485/495. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said volumes were small and some of the sales were through two north-based state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  Trade was quiet in the first half of the day except for dollar sales by a sugar exporter, a dealer with a private bank said. \par \par \uc2  The State Bank of India (SBI)  had moved with the market and was not seen actively mopping up dollars or checking the rupee's gains, he said. \par \par \uc2  The SBI sold dollars last week to meet import demand and bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected the SBI's actions to be at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behest after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) said last week it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  either directly or through SBI if the rupee came under pressure. \par \par \uc2  The RBI said it would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, premiums were off highs as Monday's aggressive paying (sell-buy swaps) did not spill over as expected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said there was normal paying for value Wednesday as banks adjusted swap positions for the month-end. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium was quoted at an annualised 5.20 percent, 10 basis points lower than Monday's close. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8v01is3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
