\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee ends off highs on light dlr buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1999\par 12:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOMBAY, Aug 31 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     came off intra-day highs towards close on Tuesday on light dollar purchases by a state-run bank, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupee ended at 43.48/485 per dollar compared with its previous close of 43.49/4925 and off 43.4675 hit in some afternoon deals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The rupee had firmed earlier on dollar sales by exporters and dealers said the state-run bank could have bought on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not head for higher levels. \par \par \uc2  The normal month-end import remittances were reduced after the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) statement last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI had said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  either directly or through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  if the rupee came under pressure. \par \par \uc2  The RBI said it would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  In the forward market, premiums ended off highs amid little paying interest (sell-buy swaps) in far forwards. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was normal paying for value Wednesday as banks adjusted swap positions for the month-end. \par \par \uc2  Call money rates remained high around ten percent but the receiving would start once they eased, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With speculation the US could raise rates once again gaining ground, after a 25 basis point hike last week, banks would prefer to swap surpluses into dollars than le