ies, mainly from foreign funds seen picking \par \par \uc2  up though they were sellers until now on uncertainty in the run \par \par \uc2  up to India's general elections. \par \par \uc2      Foreign funds have sold around $74.6 million worth of \par \par \uc2  Indian equity and debt in August after having invested nearly \par \par \uc2  one billion dollars in Indian markets in the April-July period, \par \par \uc2  but turned buyers on Wednesday and Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended Thursday firmer at 43.51/515 per dollar \par \par \uc2  against Wednesday's close of 43.52/5225, \par \par \uc2      * Forward premiums ranged as corporates pay (sell-buy \par \par \uc2  swaps) to rollover import contracts while state-run banks \par \par \uc2  receive premiums, suspected to be at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behest. \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended Thursday at an annualised \par \par \uc2  4.89 percent compared with the previous 4.8 percent. \par \par \uc2      Closing rates on Thursday: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates\tab \tab   : 7.75/8.10 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Pakistan rupee kerb closing   : 54.30/54.40\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bombay Stock index\tab \tab   : 4,846.36 (+127.36)\par     Dow Jones Indust. Avg\tab      : 11,198.45 (-127.59)\par     Hang Seng Index\tab \tab      : 13,608.38 (+129.25)\par     Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab     : 17,666.29 (-188.87)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8r01tug\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
