\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee opens easier v dlr, seen ranged. \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 1999\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee opened slightly weaker compared to its previous close and dealers said the Indian unit had adjusted for a shift in the spot date to the next week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee opened at 43.53/55 per dollar against the previous close of 43.52/5225. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee has adjusted for the Friday-Monday factor. The arbitrage has been covered," the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading of a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 9:30 a.m. (0400 GMT), the rupee was quoted at 43.53/535 per dollar, little changed from the day's open. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the rupee to weaken marginally as banks covered short dollar positions acquired on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Banks usually sell dollars on Wednesday hoping to buy them back the next two days to benefit from weekend swap differentials. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the rupee to trade in a range under the watchful eye of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Month-end dollar demand from corporates was seen continuing, but with bulk payments taken off the market, the rupee was seen trading in a range determined by the country's largest bank, the State Bank of India . \par \par \uc2  "If it weakens to 43.55, SBI will sell dollars. If it firms to 43.52, SBI will buy dollars. That essentially is going to be the story for some time now," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) on Monday said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  either directly or through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  if the rupee came under pressure and added it would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums were seen ranged amid month-end paying (sell-buy swaps) by corporates, while SBI and state-run banks were seen receiving premiums at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behest to infuse liquidity ahead of a bond auction on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will auction 11.99 percent 2009 bond worth 25 billion rupees on Friday. \par \par \uc2  THe six-month premium ended Wednesday at an annualised 4.80 percent against its previous close of 4.72 percent. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, santosh.menon@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8q01s5v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
