\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee steady, paying in short-term forwards. \b0\par\par\uc2 340 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 1999\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was steady in subdued noon trade on Wednesday and dealers said volumes were thin. \par \par \uc2  Forward dollar premiums were a bit higher on paying interest (sell-buy swaps) in the short-term sparked by the State Bank of India (SBI) , they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.52/525 per dollar at 12.30 p.m. (0700 GMT) after it opened unchanged at 43.515/525. \par \par \uc2  "There is very little corporate interest in the market. The market is a little bid (on dollars) but after the SBI's dollar sales yesterday there are not many short positions," a dealer with a state-run bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the SBI had sold dollars in the last two days to augment dollar supplies after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assured the market of its support on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) on Monday said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  either directly or through the SBI if the rupee came under pressure and added it would meet \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  "There is a lot of paying, especially last-day to last-day (August-end to September-end)," a dealer with a local swap brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  The one-month premium was quoted at an annualised 4.57 percent compared with its previous close of 4.43. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the SBI could be paying on behalf of the RBI to ensure money market liquidity was comfortable and a ten-year bond auction on Friday sailed through easily but corporates were also rolling over import contracts ahead of the month-end. \par \par \uc2  In regional markets, key Asian stock markets dipped after the U.S. FOMC hiked interest rates by 25 basis points on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Bombay stocks were off a record high of 4,813 points in noon trade. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, vidya.ranganathan@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8p01y7g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
