\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee seen ranged under  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  vigil. \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 1999\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BOMBAY, Aug 24 (Reuters) - * Indian rupee\tab \tab seen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading in a range under \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vigil after its verbal\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Monday rescued it from sliding lower, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  either directly or through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI) \par \par \uc2     if the rupee came under pressure. \par \par \uc2      It said it was willing to meet the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil and the country's debt \par \par \uc2  service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2      * The RBI statement came against the backdrop of the \par \par \uc2  rupee's slide to an all-time closing low of 43.565/57 at the \par \par \uc2  weekend. \par \par \uc2      * Dollar seen bid on month-end demand from corporates, \par \par \uc2  mainly public sector firms. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers said dollar supplies down as foreign funds lying \par \par \uc2  low in the run up to India's general elections. \par \par \uc2      Foreign funds have sold nearly $63 million worth of debt \par \par \uc2  and equity in Indian markets in August after having invested \par \par \uc2  nearly one billion dollars in the April-July period. \par \par \uc2      * Dollar sales by the country's largest bank the State Bank \par \par \uc2  of India    seen as the major source of supplies. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended Monday at 43.50/51 per dollar against \par \par \uc2  Friday's close of 43.565/57. \par \par \uc2      * Forward premiums seen tracking the spot rupee and call \par \par \uc2  money rates. \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended lower at 4.72 percent against \par \par \uc2  Friday's five percent. \par \par \uc2      Closing rates on Monday: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates\tab \tab   : 8.25/8.50 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Pakistan rupee kerb closing   : 54.10/54.15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bombay Stock index\tab \tab   : 4,729.78 (+83.97)\par     Dow Jones Indust. Avg\tab      : 11,299.76 (+.199.15)\par     Hang Seng Index\tab \tab      : 13,573.66 (+6.92)\par     Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab     : 18,233.55 (+135.44)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8o023lt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
