\par\par \b \uc2  India bonds stable on lower call, seen cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 13:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Indian government securities were stable in evening trade on Monday after an early rise on softer call money rates dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said bonds were cautious on market expectations of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after it made statements in the morning about its plan to increase dollar supplies in the market. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the rupee to turn weak and in case of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by it, rupee funds would leave the market," a primary dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Minutes before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market opened for trading on Monday, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) said it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly or sell dollars through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  in order to augment dollar supply in the market. \par \par \uc2  Bond prices had firmed up in morning deals as call money rates opened at 8.75-9.25 percent after ruling around ten percent for most of last week. \par \par \uc2  Call money was traded at 8.25-8.50 percent in closing trade, off early highs of around nine percent and compared to its previous close of 8.0-8.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was also talk of another round of federal government loan auction which kept a check on prices. \par \par \uc2  "In the past there has been a surge in prices whenever the call rates declined but today such price movement was absent," a dealer at a private bank said. \par \par \uc2  "In fact there was selling in shorter maturities which kept their prices slightly down," he said. \par \par \uc2  The 11.90 percent 2007 stock was traded at 102.95 rupees compared to Saturday's 102.90/95 while the 12.32 percent 2011 stock was quoted at 103.61/63 against 103.63/66. \par \par \uc2  The 12.50 percent 2004 security declined to 105.48/51 rupees after being dealt at 105.525 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  "There has been some outflow towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale window so traders are treading cautiously," a dealer at a large brokerage said. \par \par \uc2  The RBI on Saturday added the 11.15 percent 2002 stock to the open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  (OMO) sale list at a sale price of 101.35 rupees. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, umesh.desai@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8n0221u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
