\par\par \b \uc2  Indian rupee ends firm on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  statement. \b0\par\par\uc2 451 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 13:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 23 (Reuters) - Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  early on Monday helped the rupee end firmer after it dipped to an all time closing low at the weekend, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended at 43.50/51 per dollar after mostly trading in a range against Friday's all time closing low of 43.565/57, but off early highs of 43.49. \par \par \uc2  Minutes before trading commenced on Monday, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) said it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly or through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  in order to augment dollar supplies in the market. \par \par \uc2  The RBI said it would meet either fully or partially, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil by Indian Oil Corporation  and added it was also prepared to meet the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statements vaulted the rupee, weighed down at the weekend by rising importer dollar demand amid concerns of reduced flows into the country, to a firm start at 43.49/52 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was traded in a tight range amid SBI dollar sales, which dealers said, were executed mostly through brokers. SBI's dollar sales were maximum in the last hour of trading. \par \par \uc2  "SBI did not hit banks directly. Most of its sales were through brokers," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit an all time closing low on Friday on newspaper reports the G-8 countries could stall loans to India in reaction to its draft nuclear deterrence policy and speculation of a yuan devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said corporate demand for dollars remained good, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statements. \par \par \uc2  "Inspite of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statements which seem to suggest the rupee will not fall much from these levels, there was good demand for dollars," the chief dealer at a European bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar supplies seemed elusive with no foreign flows into the country. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) on Friday showed foreign funds sold nearly $80 million worth of debt and equity in Indian markets in August after having invested nearly one billion dollars in the April-July period. \par \par \uc2  Forward premiums ended lower on the back of a firm spot rupee and softer call money rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said premiums opened sharply lower and drifted lower amid receiving (buy-sell swaps) by some state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium ended Monday at 4.72 per dollar against the weekend's close of five percent. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, santosh.menon@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8n021w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
