\par\par \b \uc2  RBI statements propel India rupee to firm open. \b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 06:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOMBAY, Aug 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee\tab     started stronger on Monday as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issued a statement minutes before the market opened saying it was taking steps at cutting any demand supply gaps that may emerge.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupee opened at 43.49/52 per dollar against the previous close of 43.565/57, and dealers reported early deals upto 43.50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) said on Monday it was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly or sell dollars through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  in order to augment dollar supply in the market. \par \par \uc2  "Arrangements have been made by the Reserve Bank of India, to meet fully or partially, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements for the import of crude oil by Indian Oil Corporation," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in its statement. \par \par \uc2  The RBI said it was also prepared to meet the country's debt service obligations directly. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said while the statements helped the rupee open firmer, bids for the U.S unit had reappeared in early trade. \par \par \uc2  "Banks are sitting long dollars. A major sell-off now would mean hurting themselves. They will probably wait to see how corporates behave. Chances are the rupee may firm before the end of the day," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.505/52 per dollar at 9:20 a.m. (0350 GMT) and dealers said they were surprised by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves. \par \par \uc2  "Probably they see some major demand supply gaps which the market does not know about. Otherwise, these statements are most unexpected," the chief dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had probably stepped in following the rupee's fall to an all-time closing low on Friday and the sharp drop in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the week to Agust 13. \par \par \uc2  The RBI on Saturday said India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped to $33.115 billion on August 13, down from $33.410 billion in the previous week. \par \par \uc2  The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a foreign bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves were aimed at halting the slide of the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "Without these statements, the rupee would have tested 43.60 levels and moved very swiftly to its all time low of 43.70. This (the RBI's sattements) will apply the brakes," he said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's all time low of 43.70 was hit on August 19 last year. \par \par \uc2  "They probably expect uncertainty ahead of the elections. And the fact is that dollar supplies have come down sharply lately." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign institutional investors (FIIs) have been lying low in the run-up to the elections which has resulted in a sharp decline in portfolio inflows into the country. \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds sold nearly $80 million worth of debt and equity in Indian markets in August after having invested nearly $1 billion in April-July. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said forward premiums were expected to open lower tracking the spot rupee's gains and easier call money rates. \par \par \uc2  The six-month premium ended the weekend at five percent against the previous close of 4.90 percent. ((Santosh Menon, Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8n0212p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
