\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee seen in weak open,to eye SBI dlr sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 1999\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BOMBAY, Aug 23 (Reuters) - * Indian rupee\tab \tab seen in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weak open after Friday's dip to all-time closing low on fears\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  the U.S. would hold back some loans in response to the \par \par \uc2  country's recent announcement of a draft nuclear doctrine and \par \par \uc2  speculation of a yuan devaluation, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * Rupee to trade in a weaker range and test 43.60 levels in \par \par \uc2  early trade, they added. \par \par \uc2      * Dollar demand seen good as cautious corporates cover \par \par \uc2  exposures following the unexpected rupee slide late last week, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2      * While the pressure is building for China to devalue the \par \par \uc2  yuan, faced with a slackening economy and declining exports, \par \par \uc2  analysts said they did not see it happening before the \par \par \uc2  beginning of the next year. \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen keeping a sharp eye on the rupee and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through its surrogate, the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  , in the event of a sharp rupee slide, they said. \par \par \uc2      * Early SBI dollar sales may force banks to cut long \par \par \uc2  positions and help rupee recover, they said. \par \par \uc2      * Dollar supplies seen down amid low fresh portfolio \par \par \uc2  investment flows as foreign funds lie low in the run up to \par \par \uc2  India's general elections. \par \par \uc2      Foreign funds sold nearly $80 million worth of debt and \par \par \uc2  equity in Indian markets in August after having invested nearly \par \par \uc2  one billion dollars in the April-July period. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers say exporters seen delaying dollar sales after \par \par \uc2  rupee's rather unexpected weakness. \par \par \uc2      * India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell $298 million to \par \par \uc2  $33.115 billion on August 13 from $33.410 billion in the \par \par \uc2  previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its \par \par \uc2  weekly statistical supplement on Saturday. \par \par \uc2  * The year-on-year M3 money supply growth was steady at \par \par \uc2  18.5 percent in the two weeks to July 30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  * India's year-on-year inflation rate measured by the \par \par \uc2  wholesale price index rose to 1.70 percent in the week ended \par \par \uc2  August 7 from 1.62 percent in the previous week, the Industry \par \par \uc2  Ministry said on Sunday. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended at an all-time low on Friday at 43.565/57 \par \par \uc2  per dollar against Thursday close of 43.48/49. \par \par \uc2      * Forward premiums seen higher tracking the spot rupee amid \par \par \uc2  cautious paying by corporates. \par \par \uc2      * The six-month premium ended higher on Friday at five \par \par \uc2  percent against its previous close 4.90 percent. \par \par \uc2      Closing rates at weekend: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates\tab \tab   : 8.0/8.50 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Pakistan rupee kerb closing   : 54.07/54.12\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bombay Stock index\tab \tab   : 4,645.81 (+15.75)\par     Dow Jones Indust. Avg\tab      : 11,100.61 (+136.77)\par     Hang Seng Index\tab \tab      : 13,566.74 (+163.15)\par     Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab     : 18,098.11 (+218.37)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bomba