\par\par \b \uc2  India call money above nine pct, rupee weighs. \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1999\par 06:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 11 (Reuters) - Indian call money was traded in in higher ranges in opening deals on Wednesday, with sentiment affected by heightened tension with Pakistan after the downing of a Pakistani military aircraft, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Fighters of the Indian air force shot down a Pakistani maritime reconnaissance aircraft on Tuesday saying it intruded into its airspace, a claim denied by Pakistan which accused its neighbour and arch-foe of downing the plane without any provocation. \par \par \uc2  The tension affected sentiment, already hit by reduced liquidity in the past few days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Call money was traded at 9.10-9.40 percent compared with Tuesday's close of 8.8-9.10. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the deals are getting done at 9.20 percent," a dealer with a private bank said. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity was strained by outflows of 30 billion rupees into a 10-year bond auction last week and a further 20-25 billion into the Reserve Bank of India's (RBI) open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The pressure on the rupee is complicating matters further. The market feels state-run banks, which normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on the RBI's behalf, will lend less," a dealer with a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.485/495 per dollar at 10:05 a.m. (0435 GMT) after it opened at 43.45/50, weaker than Tuesday's close of 43.425/43. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee could weaken further if the tension with Pakistan escalates. \par \par \uc2  Pakistan's Foreign Minister Sartaj Aziz told Reuters Television on Wednesday his country's armed forces were on full alert and said India should apologise for its action. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday evening, Aziz had said Pakistan reserved the right to make an appropriate response to the Indian action. \par \par \uc2  Money market liquidity would be further hit if the RBI sells dollars through state-run banks to defend the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it has done in the past, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The spot date for today falls on the reporting Friday, so even if there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  there should be no major impact on liquidity," a dealer with a state-run bank said. \par \par \uc2  Banks report two-weekly positions to the RBI on alternate Fridays and maintain cash reserve ratios over the two-week period. The next reporting day is August 13. \par \par \uc2  "But it is likely the availability of funds has been affected by their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, the spot date for which falls today," he added. \par \par \uc2  The rupee had slipped to intra-day lows of 43.585 on Monday before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the State Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SBI)  helped it recover. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv8b02q9g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
