\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  dents  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  reserves. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1999\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, June 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $200 million in the third week of June, reflecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cool the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market hit by the Kashmir crisis. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Saturday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were $33.289 billion on June 18, down from the week-ago level of $33.489 billion. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the drop was expected after RBI Governor Bimal Jalan said on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars to the state-run State Bank of India , the country's largest commercial bank, last week. \par \par \uc2  In a statement released at a conference on rural development, Jalan said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had deliberately followed a policy of keeping reserves at a very high level and the RBI bought dollars from the market in March, April and May. \par \par \uc2  "In fact, we bought as much as $2.5 billion during these three months. Last week, however, RBI sold dollars to SBI (State Bank of India) in order to meet some extra demand," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement quoting the governor said. \par \par \uc2  The statement rescued the rupee from its 10-month lows of 43.43. It closed at 43.315/33 per dollar on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The rupee has weakened by more than one percent since late May when news of the conflict in Kashmir first hit financial markets. \par \par \uc2  India has been fighting what it says are Pakistani infiltrators and Islamic guerrillas on its side of the military control line in the Himalayan territory of Kashmir for the past one month. \par \par \uc2  The situation put investors in a cautious mood and increased corporate demand for dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The Kashmir conflict is driving importers to increase their hedging horizons and cover ratios. The RBI's decision to sell dollars is to curb any excessive volatility or undue bearishness on the rupee," said Vasan Shridharan, Treasury Economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  Jalan was quoted as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to keep a watch on the markets. \par \par \uc2  "Except for some temporary hiccups, financial markets are functioning normally and overall conditions are satisfactory. RBI will continue to monitor the position and as in the past take appropriate measures when necessary," the RBI statement said. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy is to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets orderly and meet as necessary temporary demand-supply gaps that emerge from time to time," it said. \par \par \uc2  While the depletion in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets was $200 million, dealers said it was likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold a lot more and adjusted the spot position by receiving forward dollar premiums (buy-sell swaps). ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6q05m6k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
