\par\par \b \uc2  Fears of Indian Ctrl Bk Action Seen Limiting Rupee Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1999\par 16:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--Fears that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem any dramatic slide of the Indian rupee (INR) will likely limit the fall of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank of India will support the rupee through the State Bank of India," a dealer at a foreign bank said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the Indian rupee (INR) slipped sharply in late trade to close at a new low of INR43.025 to the dollar compared with INR42.83 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  The impact of political developments on the rupee is of concern as the reaction of the bond market is directly linked to this market as well. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday, Indian forces began air strikes in the northern province of Kashmir, close to Pakistan, against what it called Pakistan-backed infiltrators in the region. Thursday, Pakistan said it shot down two Indian aircraft. \par \par \uc2  Since recent tensions on the border between the two countries began Wednesday morning, the rupee has fallen 0.64% while the Sensex, India's benchmark stock index, has fallen 4.9%. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has on two separate occasions stemmed the slide of the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by withdrawing facilities to banks and companies and raising short-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  In fact, conviction that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't allow the rupee to slip sharply has prompted smaller importers to stay unhedged in the market. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have also reiterated from time to time that they will ensure orderly conditions in the market without targeting a specific level for the rupee. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they see the State Bank of India selling dollars in early trade to prevent volatility. " I see the RBI (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) selling when the rupee touches INR43.50, not before that," the chief dealer at an American bank said. He added that there were corporate dollar sales late Wednesday and early Thursday which helped the rupee recover, but said that it wasn't likely to happen Friday. \par \par \uc2  "In fact, the same guys who sold this morning (Thursday) will be the first ones to buy back their dollars," he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramya Venugopal; 91 22 2884211; rvenugopal@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-05-99 \par \par \uc2  1405GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5r044h8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
