\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Opens Steady; Ctrl Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1999\par 06:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee opened steady against the dollar Tuesday and is expected to continue to trade in a narrow range on lack of both corporate and interbank interest, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Tuesday between 42.735-42.745 rupees, unchanged from Monday's close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar supplies continue to flow into the market only to be absorbed by one or two large state-owned banks acting at the behest of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is said to be holding the rupee steady by mopping up these excess dollars through large state-owned banks. \par \par \uc2  This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep the spot dollar in a narrow range. With importers preferring to stay unhedged, demand for the dollar is expected to be dull. And as is always the trend in a stable rupee market, there are more exporters looking to sell dollars than there are buyers of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  According to the latest available figures from the Reserve Bank of India, the central banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves touched a record high of $33.25 billion May 15. \par \par \uc2  Dealers put the range for the dollar Tuesday between INR42.73 and INR42.76 during the day. \par \par \uc2  - By Ramya Venugopal; 91 22 2884211; rvenugopal@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 25-05-99 \par \par \uc2  0403GMT \par \par \uc2  2506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv5p03wt9\par }\page {\par\