\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee seen weak before trust vote,eye on RBI. \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 1999\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2     BOMBAY, April 15 (Reuters) - * Indian rupee seen under \par \par \uc2  pressure to weaken on Thursday on political uncertainty as the \par \par \uc2  year-old Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) led coalition faces a \par \par \uc2  confidence vote later in the day, dealers say. \par \par \uc2      * Indian President asked Prime Minister Atal Behari \par \par \uc2  Vajpayee to seek a confidence vote in parliament after a key \par \par \uc2  ally of the government withdrew support to it on Wednesday. The \par \par \uc2  government will announce at 11:00 a.m. it is seeking the vote, \par \par \uc2  Information and Broadcasting Minister Pramod Mahajan said. \par \par \uc2      * Early dollar bids could weaken rupee to 43 levels, but \par \par \uc2  the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) seen checking volatility \par \par \uc2  through direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or through state-run banks. \par \par \uc2      * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sitting on a record levels of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves which stood at $32.535 billion on April 1 \par \par \uc2  against $31.586 billion in the previous week. \par \par \uc2      * Dealers say importer covering unlikely to be much as \par \par \uc2  corporates already well covered, but dollar supplies seen \par \par \uc2  contracting as exporters delay hedging receivables. \par \par \uc2      * The rupee ended Tuesday weaker at 42.74/75 per dollaer \par \par \uc2  against Monday's close of 42.685/695 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      * The six month premium ended at an annualised 7.13 percent \par \par \uc2  against 7.0 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2      * Banks and financial markets were shut on Wednesday for a \par \par \uc2  local holiday. . Previous closing rates: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Call money rates\tab \tab   : 7.70-7.90 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Pakistan rupee (kerb) v dlr   : 51.70/51.80\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bombay Stock index\tab \tab   : 3,464.42 (+0.75)\par     Dow Jones Indust. Avg\tab      : 10,411.66 (+16.65)\par     Hang Seng Index\tab \tab      : 11,834.13 (-65.56)\par     Nikkei 225 Index\tab \tab     : 16,764.68 (+49.52)\par     FTSE 100\tab \tab \tab \tab : 6,493.6 (-19.5)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Santosh Menon, Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4f032cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
