\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Ends Flat; Lower Co Demand, Ctrl Bk Sales Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 1999\par 14:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee ended steady and regained early losses against the dollar on long selling by banks and reduced demand from importers, dealers said Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at INR42.67-42.6850, around its Tuesday close of INR42.67. The dollar touched a high of INR42.76 in early trade Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Rumors that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling forward dollars deliverable in June also helped ease the pressure on the rupee, dealers said. The Reserve Bank of India declined to confirm or deny the rumor. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said it wasn't clear yet whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to steady the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We are asking around but haven't been able to get a confirmation from any bank," the chief dealer at a large U.S-based bank said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was less apprehensive Wednesday of the political threats to the federal government, bankers said, explaining the rupee's recovery. \par \par \uc2  The rupee lost 0.6% of its value against the dollar Tuesday when banks and importers bought dollars heavily on political concerns. \par \par \uc2  The All India Anna Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam, a key ally of the ruling coalition, recalled its ministers Monday and threatened to withdraw support from the government when the parliament reconvenes next week. The AIADMK had demanded the resignation of the defense minister, who belongs to another party in the coalition. The Bharatiya Janata Party, which leads the ruling coalition, has so far shown no signs of compromise. \par \par \uc2  Exporters also took advantage of the dollar's rise and sold dollars, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Rupee premiums on the forward dollar ended lower because of the stronger rupee and lower interbank overnight call rate. \par \par \uc2  The premium on the six-month forward dollar closed unchanged at 7.1%. \par \par \uc2  Overnight call money rates slipped to 5.50%-5.75% after the market saw inflows to the tune of INR47 billion. Most of the trades on Wednesday were done at 7.00%. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers said the rupee is expected to trade between INR42.65-42.75 unless there are further political developments. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramya Venugopal; 91 22 2884211; rvenugopal@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 07-04-99 \par \par \uc2  1201GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv4702lkz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
