\par\par \b \uc2  Indian Rupee Opens Slightly Weaker; Seen Range-Bound \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 1998\par 05:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee (INR) opened slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar Monday, with dealers predicting range-bound trading. While some dollar supplies are expected this week on unwinding of long-dollar positions by banks, the month-end demand from customers is expected to balance the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened Monday at INR42.29-.31, slightly stronger than Friday's close at INR42.28-.29. \par \par \uc2  The rupee is expected to trade in a tight range for a few days, mainly on fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has, on two occasions, raised short-term interest rates and withdrawn facilities to companies to halt a run on the rupee. Because of this, market players will think twice before pulling the rupee down, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank, has also been keeping the rupee in a range over the past few weeks. State Bank's actions are significant because the market perceives them to be on behalf of the Reserve Bank of India. \par \par \uc2  Some participants are holding long-dollar positions, dealers said. The rupee weakened considerably, to INR42.41, Friday as banks took long-dollar positions, anticipating heavy corporate demand. They expected their customers to buy dollars in reaction to the lowering of India's sovereign rating by international credit-ratings agency, Standard & Poor's late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, State Bank of India came in selling dollars and pulled the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to INR42.28. As a result, some banks held on to their long positions over the weekend. The unwinding of these positions is expected to bring in some dollars, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  These supplies can be expected to prop up the rupee, they added. However, it is not clear if the State Bank of India, under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's instruction, will allow the rupee to move up too much, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  For latest indicative rupee rates please see Telerate page [26501]. \par \par \uc2  -By Ramya Venugopal; 91 22 2884211-18; rvenugopal@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  26-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0442GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914duaq00x1v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
