\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Monetary Measures For  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Welcome -Exec \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 1998\par 10:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HYDERABAD, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Vysya Bank Chairman K. Ramamoorthy said Friday that the Reserve Bank of India's recent measures using monetary policy instead of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control a fall in the value of the rupee (INR) ($1=INR42.46) versus the U.S. dollar was a welcome change. \par \par \uc2  He said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must at some point put a stop to the use of an increase in rupee resources by market participants to engage in arbitrage in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The RBI in August reduced liquidity and raised interest rates to restrict the rupee's fall against the dollar when the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breached record lows, touching INR43.70. The RBI's measures stabilized the rupee at around INR42.50 against the dollar, and the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained around that level since. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is like "riding two tigers," Ramamoorthy said, adding that it's a tough job to simultaneously stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  level and maintain liquidity at a comfortable level. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  02-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0812GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914dua200vxj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict