\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Reserve/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  -2: Small Volumes Traded \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 1998\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's minimal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was symbolic - a signal to the market that they won't let the rupee premiums on the forward dollar to decline. \par \par \uc2  Thursday the Reserve Bank of India's adopted measures to stop the rupee slide and check speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank increased banks' cash reserve ratio to 11% from 10% and increased the rate on its sale of repurchase agreements of government securities to 8% from 5%, reducing liquidity and raising interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "The Reserve Bank wants to keep the premiums on forward dollars up to dissuade banks to go long on the dollar," said a dealer at a state owned bank. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is trading at INR42.57-.58, much lower than its Thursday close of INR42.78-.88. The dollar had opened steady at INR42.85-.88. \par \par \uc2  The rupee premium on forward dollars for delivery at the end of September rose to INR0.74-0.79 after the Reserve Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from its earlier level of INR0.65-0.70. The premium for September dollars had closed Thursday at INR0.75-0.95. \par \par \uc2  For latest indicative rupee rates, please see Telerate page [26501]. \par \par \uc2  -By Raghavendra Upadhyaya; (91 22) 288-4211 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0956GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8l0751k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley