\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee ends sharply firmer on RBI support. \b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 1998\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 20 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended firmer on Thursday after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the spot and swap markets and also announced a package of measures in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended at 42.80/90 per dollar against its previous close of 43.47/53 and after volatile trade ranging between a record low of 43.70 and an intra-day high of 42.60. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee's slide to its lifetime low of 43.70 was first halted by RBI enquiries about rates, followed by direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through spot dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  A series of measures announced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later accelerated the rupee's rise and helped it reverse a three-day losing patch earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  At its lowest on Thursday, the rupee had lost around 1.4 percent from its weekend close. \par \par \uc2  The RBI announced a 100 basis point increase in banks' cash reserve ratio (CRR) to 11 percent from August 29 and hiked its repo rate to eight percent from five. \par \par \uc2  Other measures included a warning to exporters not to delay their remittances and a requirement that banks report their end-of-day positions and intra-day peak positions. \par \par \uc2  "Overall the measures reversed sentiment to a large extent and should keep the rupee stable for some time to come," said a dealer at a private bank. \par \par \uc2  "People are now going to be more careful about taking the rupee up or down. We should see only back-to-back covering of trade transactions for some time now," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI's moves came when dollar demand had picked up on statements by Commerce Minister Ramakrishna Hedge that the rupee could weaken further by around one percent and that India was unlikely to reach its 1998/99 (April-March) exports growth target of 20 percent. \par \par \uc2  Forward dollar premiums flared up sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paid (bought dollars in the swap market), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "RBI paid in September," said a dealer. Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also paid in October-dollars. \par \par \uc2  The annualised premium on six-month dollars ended at 12.43 percent against Wednesday's clsoe of 9.08. Premiums for other months also rose although they dipped slightly towards close, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The uptick was particularly sharp for near months," said a dealer. "It looks like RBI wants forward premiums to be a bit firm to prevent a rush for cover by importers." \par \par \uc2  "Current levels are also attractive for receiving and we may see exporters coming in now," he said. "Premiums should start easing in a couple of days." ((Giri Venkatesan, Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8k018ci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
