\par\par \b \uc2  India Rupee Closes Dn Despite Reserve Bank Gov Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 13:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BOMBAY (Dow Jones)--Dollar buying by State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank, created panic in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, pushing the rupee (INR) to new lows and forcing the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor to verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and support the rupee, dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Bimal Jalan said Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take appropriate steps, including monetary measures, when necessary. \par \par \uc2  However, the nervousness in the market continued when State Bank of India asked for dollar quotes from several banks in late afternoon trading. Banks - assuming State Bank will buy dollars - panicked and bought dollars to cover short positions. \par \par \uc2  Their dollar-buying pushed the rupee to new lows, albeit briefly, leading the dollar to trade at a high of INR43.66 in intraday trading. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended at a record closing low of INR43.50-.51, up from its previous close of INR43.36 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "When State Bank along with others actually sold (dollars) near close of trading, the rupee quickly regained part of its losses," said a dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the State Bank dollar selling near close of trading could be have been prompted by the Reserve Bank of India's dollar sales directly to them. \par \par \uc2  Sometimes the Reserve Bank doesn't like to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly by selling dollars in the market because it creates panic and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen on avoiding a volatile market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  19-08-98 \par \par \uc2  1120GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du8j00rrp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
