\par\par \b \uc2  India Fin Adviser -2: Speaking At Govt Meeting \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 1998\par 09:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI (Dow Jones)--The recent fall in the Indian rupee to record lows below INR43.40 in early trading Wednesday doesn't reflect a sharp depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the government's chief economic adviser who was attending a meeting of customs officers. \par \par \uc2  Since August 1997, the rupee has depreciated around 17.5%, and in the past two weeks has dropped from INR42.50 to INR43.43 currently. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the fall in the rupee has been sharp," said Finance Adviser Shankar Acharya, who is also acting Finance Secretary, following the transfer of Montek Singh Ahluwalia from that position last week. \par \par \uc2  He noted the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mandated to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at any time it feels the value of the rupee should be supported. \par \par \uc2  He also said the devaluation of the Russian ruble won't hurt Indian trade. \par \par \uc2  "There will be no significant" drop-off in exports to Russia because of an agreement with Russia to fix the rupee-ruble exchange rate, Acharya also said. But he noted that the devaluation of the Russian ruble affects markets worldwide and does increase uncertainty in that regard. \par \par \uc2  Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday cut the lower limit of the ruble (RUR) band to RUR9.5 to the dollar from RUR6.3 to the dollar previously. \par \par \uc2  In 1992, India and Russia agreed to a rupee-ruble rate at 19.1 rupees to the ruble for the repayment of INR310 billion, about $7.14 billion, in debt accrued by India for the purchase of defense equipment and other items from the former Soviet Union. The debt is auctioned by the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Russian importers who can obtain letters of credit and buy goods denominated in rupees from Indian exporters. The Indian exporters then receive payment from the Reserve Bank of India. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-08-98 \par \par \uc2  0714GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8j071za\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
