\par\par \b \uc2  FEATURE - India rupee braces for more pain. \b0\par\par\uc2     By Giri Venkatesan \par \uc2 855 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 1998\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      BOMBAY, Aug 17 (Reuters) - A mood of uncertainty and unease \par \par \uc2  is palpable among India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market players as they brace \par \par \uc2  for the next likely burst of volatility to hit the rupee. \par \par \uc2      The rupee hit its lifetime low of 43.35 to the dollar on \par \par \uc2  August 12 before paring some of its losses but traders say \par \par \uc2  further falls lie in store. The rupee was quoted at 43.20/21 on \par \par \uc2  Monday morning. \par \par \uc2      "Basically, we have to realise that India is a \par \par \uc2  dollar-deficit country," said the corporate treasury head of a \par \par \uc2  western-India based textile firm. \par \par \uc2      The rupee's trend will therefore always tend to be bearish. \par \par \uc2      "What happens is that events - political uncertainty, \par \par \uc2  regional market developments, bad news in general such as the \par \par \uc2  ratings downgrade - these determine how bearish this sentiment \par \par \uc2  gets to be and this will determine the rupee's rate of fall." \par \par \uc2      SHARP FALL IN PAST YEAR, MORE PRESSURE SEEN \par \par \uc2      The wheel has turned full circle for the Indian rupee and \par \par \uc2  its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year. \par \par \uc2      On August 15, 1997, Reserve Bank of India (RBI) deputy \par \par \uc2  governor Y.V. Reddy said the rupee appeared to be overvalued \par \par \uc2  based on real effective exchange rate data. \par \par \uc2      The RBI was then buying dollars to prevent the rupee \par \par \uc2  appreciating and analysts were concerned over how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would manage strong capital inflows. \par \par \uc2      A slowing economy also hit domestic dollar demand and \par \par \uc2  helped the rupee. \par \par \uc2      One year later, the rupee has fallen more than 17 percent. \par \par \uc2      And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold dollars a number of times to \par \par \uc2  check speculative attacks on the rupee. \par \par \uc2      On Friday, the RBI again warned rupee bears not to \par \par \uc2  speculate against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Yashwant Sinha \par \par \uc2  also stressed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check \par \par \uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  Poor exports and foreign investor unease, particularly \par \par \uc2  since India conducted nuclear tests in May, mean that a country \par \par \uc2  which has traditionally relied on foreign capital flows to \par \par \uc2  bridge its current account deficit must brace itself for \par \par \uc2  pressure on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  NUCLEAR-BLASTS, SANCTIONS HAVE MORE IMPACT THAN ASIA CRISIS \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the rupee's fall, it lost about 10 percent \par \par \uc2  between August 1997 and May 1998," said K.N. Dey, senior \par \par \uc2  vice-president at Mecklai Financial & Commercial Services, a \par \par \uc2  risk management advisory firm. \par \par \uc2      "But it has fallen more than seven percent in the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  period," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out two sets of nuclear tests in May, after a \par \par \uc2  24-year gap, triggering major economic powers to slap \par \par \uc2  sanctions. \par \par \uc2      Investor worries over the country were not helped by a \par \par \uc2  sovereign credit rating downgrade to junk bond status in June. \par \par \uc2      And it is these two factors which have concerned analysts \par \par \uc2  most. \par \par \uc2      "Actually, despite political uncertainty the rupee was \par \par \uc2  pretty steady till May," Dey said. \par \par \uc2      General elections earlier this year in the world's most \par \par \uc2  populous democracy were inconclusive and analysts had feared \par \par \uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would react negatively to the uncertainty \par \par \uc2  inherent in a fragile minority coalition. \par \par \uc2  FALL CUSHIONED BY GOOD MANAGEMENT BY RBI, CAPITAL CONTROLS \par \par \uc2  While the rupee has fallen, it has been shielded from the \par \par \uc2  steep falls of other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  thanks to fairly \par \par \uc2  strong external account indicators, the presence of capital \par \par \uc2  controls and some deft exchange rate management by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  India's current account deficit for 1997/98 (April-March) \par \par \uc2  was around 1.7 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) while \par \par \uc2  the short-term component in its total external debt was less \par \par \uc2  than 20 percent. \par \par \uc2      India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, at $27.09 billion on \par \par \uc2  July 31, are enough to cover six months' imports, analysts say. \par \par \uc2      The rupee not being fully convertible on the capital \par \par \uc2  account has also made it less susceptible to speculative \par \par \uc2  attacks. \par \par \uc2      "Speculative attacks could be more severe if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  is fully convertible," Dey said. "But in India there is a limit \par \par \uc2  to the speculative positions that traders can take." \par \par \uc2      But poor exports are a cause for concern and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it expects the current account deficit to widen \par \par \uc2  to two percent of GDP this year. \par \par \uc2      Exports declined by almost 8 percent between April-June \par \par \uc2  1998 from the year earlier period. And RBI's Reddy said on \par \par \uc2  Friday a poor forecast for global trade for the year reduced \par \par \uc2  the scope for Indian exports to grow. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN SNEEZES, CHINA CATCHES A COLD, INDIA SHIVERS \par \par \uc2  The headline in a local daily last week sums up India's \par \par \uc2  current predicament. \par \par \uc2      The latest plunge in the rupee comes as fears over regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  grow after the yen hit eight-year lows. \par \par \uc2      Analysts say local sentiment remains nervous as the \par \par \uc2  Japanese yen holds weak and amid uncertainties over a possible \par \par \uc2  devaluation of the Chinese yuan. \par \par \uc2      But analysts say capital flows remain the main concern for \par \par \uc2  the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "Sentiment of course will be affected if the yuan is \par \par \uc2  devalued but for me the biggest worry is over capital inflows," \par \par \uc2  said Vasan Shridharan, treasury economist at Standard Chartered \par \par \uc2  Bank in Bombay. \par \par \uc2  ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, \par \par \uc2  Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8h00y7j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
