\par\par \b \uc2  India spot rupee off lows, dollar premiums up. \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee recovered from an intra-day low but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained under pressure on Thursday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Players were cautious about likely \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , political and regional developments, they said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 43.15/18 per dollar in dull trade in the afternoon, off its intra-day low of 43.25. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the undercurrent was still very bearish for the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "We've been advised to buy dollars by the banks who are all very bearish," said the head of a corporate treasury. \par \par \uc2  Heavy corporate demand led to the rupee's sharp fall on Wednesday when it touched an all-time low of 43.35 in volatile trade, and it took several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) to help it to a firmer close at 42.95/05. \par \par \uc2  "After Wednesday's hectic trading and wild movements, the market is slightly calm today," said a dealer with a local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage. \par \par \uc2  The forward premiums on the dollar were higher at the short end with the one and six month levels at 9.28 and 9.30 respectively against the previous close of 8.11 and 9.02. \par \par \uc2  "Near-term paying interest (buying of dollars in swap market) has emerged on fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will resort to tightening of liquidity to support the rupee," said a dealer with a private bank. \par \par \uc2  In the overseas markets, the dollar was stronger against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on concerns about the Russian economy, the rouble's possible devaluation and Hongkong's falling stock markets. \par \par \uc2  "The rupee is unlikely to be influenced by the rouble since our trade ties with them are minimal and restricted to the escrow account," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some of the concerns on the political front had eased after reports that a key ally of the ruling coalition had deferred its decision to withdraw support. \par \par \uc2  The ally had been upset that a regional river waters dispute had not been setlled as per their wishes. \par \par \uc2  Offshore, the rupee was at 46.30/50 for the six month non-deliverable forward (NDF) dollar, unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said much of the corporate forward dollar demand on Wednesday had been fuelled by the high spreads between onshore and offshore rupee markets. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8d032ap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
