\par\par \b \uc2  India rupee ends weak, off record low on RBI sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1998\par 13:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, Aug 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee ended weaker against the dollar on Wednesday in volatile trade, but was off its record low of 43.35 on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The rupee ended at a record low of 42.95/05 per dollar against its previous close of 42.88/91. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rupee weakened sharply to hit an all-time low of 43.35 during the day on heavy corporate demand in the spot and forward markets, but several rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) helped it cut part of the losses. \par \par \uc2  The previous low was on June 23 when the rupee briefly crossed the 43 level after Moody's Investors Services downgraded India's rating following the May nuclear tests and subsequent imposition of economic sanctions. \par \par \uc2  The rupee's fall on Wednesday was on account of heavy bidding for the dollar from local corporates and a spillover of public sector demand which has been seen for the past few days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Initially it was one large corporate buying dollars and after some time even the smaller ones joined in," said a treasury-marketing executive. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the fall in premiums on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas non-deliverable forward (NDF) markets could have triggered some local forward demand. \par \par \uc2  "Despite Asia's economic woes, traders felt that offshore premiums were slightly overdone," said a dealer at an overseas bank. \par \par \uc2  Regional markets have been affected in the recent past by Japan's economic and banking woes, the falling Japanese yen and fears of devaluation in China and Hongkong. \par \par \uc2  "Indian corporates would have started buying onshore and selling offshore on the view that the rupee NDF premiums would come off," he added. \par \par \uc2  The rupee was quoted at 46.30/50 for the six month NDF dollar - a spread of 1.35 rupees higher than the domestic rupee on Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  Another factor fuelling the rupee's fall was the political instability, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  India's ruling coalition is facing problems with two of its regional allies having threatened to withdraw support if their demands were not met. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the RBI came into the market several times today, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  both verbally and by selling dollars themselves and through the State Bank of India (SBI). \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the SBI sold dollars in the first half of the day at 42.98, but after the 43 level was breached the SBI turned a buyer of dollars and this led to a sharp fall in the rupee. \par \par \uc2  "The SBI was selling (dollars) again at 43.20 but only the RBI's enquiries could check the rupee's decline," said a dealer at a local \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  brokerage. \par \par \uc2  The rupee recorded a historic low of 43.35 before the retracement, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The forward premium on the dollar ended up at 8.11 percent and 9.02 percent for the one and six months respectively against the previous close of 5.64 and 8.20. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said enquiries by the RBI and receiving (selling dollars in swap market) by the SBI guided premiums to a lower close from their intra-day highs hit after the rupee's sharp fall. \par \par \uc2  ((Vidya Ranganathan, Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8c02ypt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi