\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - Indian newspapers - June 22. \b0\par\par\uc2 832 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Following is a summary of major Indian business and political stories in leading newspapers prepared for REUTERS by Business News and Information Services Pvt Ltd, New Delhi Tel:3326806, 3326813, 3326849 Fax:+91-11-3351006 E-mail: biznis@giasdl01.vsnl.net.in \par \par \uc2  Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  - oo0oo- \par \par \uc2  TOP STORIES \par \par \uc2  Indian Express \par \par \uc2  INDIA, RUSSIA SIGN NUCLEAR POWER DEAL \par \par \uc2  Russia and India have signed an accord to build India's first large-scale nuclear power station. Russian atomic energy minister Yevgeni Adamov and chief of India's Atomic Energy Commission R.Chidambaram signed a pact to cooperate in building two 1,000 megawatt nuclear power reactors at Kudankulam in Tamil Nadu. With this, the nearly two-and-a-half decade of ban imposed by western countries limiting India's access to atomic energy cooperation have come to an end. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  The Pioneer \par \par \uc2  STATE GOVERNMENTS WON'T BE SACRIFICED: ADVANI \par \par \uc2  Federal Home Minister Lal Krishna Advani ruled out the dismissal of any state government merely to ensure survival of the coalition government at the Centre. But Advani justified his decision to send fact-finding teams to Bihar and West Bengal. Advani's statement comes in the wake of a threat by ruling party's key ally All India Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam to withdraw support if the Tamil Nadu government was not dismissed. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  The Economic Times \par \par \uc2  COGENTRIX TO REPLACE U.S. FIRM WITH EUROPEAN \par \par \uc2  U.S. power developer Cogentrix has initiated moves to replace the U.S. firm with a European firm for handling the boiler contract at its power plant at Mangalore. The switch-over was being done to work around the U.S. sanctions and, according to sources, could be the first U.S. casualty in infrastructure sector. Several U.S. companies' projects in India are backed by U.S. Exim exposures. Cogentrix is developing a 1,000-megawatts Mangalore plant, one of the seven fast-track power projects. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  RUPEE DIP: FOREIGN DEBT UP \par \par \uc2  India's external debt burden has moved up by around 440 billion rupees in the past eight months due to the 15 percent depreciation of the rupee against the dollar. But the movement of other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar has reduced the country's external debt burden in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A finance ministry status report on India's external debt put the external debt at $92.880 bilion as of end-September 1997. \par \par \uc2  -. \par \par \uc2  Financial Express \par \par \uc2  INDO-OMAN REJECTS UHDE'S LOWER OFFER FOR UREA PROJECT \par \par \uc2  Indo-Oman Fertiliser Co. has rejected Uhde GmbH's offer to lower its bid for the 32-bilion-rupee ($800-million) turnkey tender for urea-ammonia project by 3.2 bilion rupees. Uhde's offer was seen as a last-ditch attempt by the German multinational to wrest the project from Italy's Snamprogetti which has been shortlisted for the contract. The reduced offer would have improved on Snamprogetti's leveraged bid by over 2.4 billion rupees. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  RESERVE BANK MAY STEP IN TO STEM RUPEE SLIDE \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to check any slide of the rupee in the aftermath of Moody's downgrade. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already discounted the downgrade. Banking sources said the the market was nervous and Moody's two-notch downgrade was unexpected. Exporters have already decided to hold on to dollars after the new downgrades, they added. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  Business Standard \par \par \uc2  GOVERNMENT WORKS ON TWO-PRONGED STRATEGY \par \par \uc2  The government will go in for more political dialogue, particularly with the G-8 countries, and a series of new policy initiatives to bolster foreign investor sentiment. India is also expected to play down its belligerent approach and opt for more behind-the-scenes negotiations. The diplomatic offensive will seek to persuade members of the Group of Eight to soften their hardline stand on multilateral loans to India, which, at present, have been deferred. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  INFLATION RATE COMES DOWN TO 6.54 PCT \par \par \uc2  The annual rate of inflation came down marginally by 0.13 percentage point to 6.54 percent for the week ended June 6, despite increase in prices of petrol and urea in the Budget. The inflation, based on the wholesale price index (WPI), stood at 6.54 percent (provisional) for the week compared to 6.67 percent in the previous week and 5.63 percent in the corresponding week of the previous year. Surprisingly, the hikes in petrol and urea prices, which were later rolled back, did not influence the WPI. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  The Observer \par \par \uc2  GOVERNMENT TO CONTEST EU DECISION \par \par \uc2  India will contest the European Union's decision to levy contervailing duty on imports of broad-spectrum antibiotics originating from India. India's case would be presented at the Brussels during the bilateral meet scheduled for end-June. Officials said the European Union has not taken into account all the facts provided by the India while arriving at its decision. \par \par \uc2  -. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02d6v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
