\par\par \b \uc2  India reserves to show small drop in 3rd week June. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Santosh Menon \par \uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1998\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BOMBAY, June 22 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will only show a small decline in the third week of June after registering a $1.19 billion drop in the first two weeks, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  source told Reuters on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to moderate the rupee's slide against the dollar, largely operating through State Bank of India, the country's largest public sector comercial bank, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There will not be much depletion seen when figures are released for that period," the RBI source said on Monday, referring to the week through June 19. \par \par \uc2  India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $1.19 billion to $27.57 billion in the two-week period to June 12 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $909 million during the second week of June. \par \par \uc2  The reserves had fallen by $258 million during the first week to June 5. \par \par \uc2  The sources pointed out the reserves were still $215 million higher than December 1997 levels, when the rupee was reeling in the wake of the South-East Asian crisis. \par \par \uc2  The rupee lost over 60 paise in value after it weakened to 42.85 per dollar in Monday mid-morning deals in reaction to a fresh wave of bearish sentiment after Moody's Investors Service demoted India's credit rating by two notches to below investment grade on Friday evening. \par \par \uc2  There was little sign of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Monday morning trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Over 6.5 percent has been chipped off the rupee during May and June after the Indian unit was lashed by a wave of bearish sentiments following India's nuclear tests carried out last month. ((Bombay newsroom, +91 22 265-9000 fax +91 22 264-1699, Bombay.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6m02d10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
