\par\par \b \uc2  India  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves edge up after fall week ago. \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 1998\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW DELHI, June 1 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose slightly in the week ended May 22 after a sharp fall the previous week and bankers said it was an indication the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had stabilised after initial panic. \par \par \uc2  India's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $25.52 billion on May 22, a $53 million increase over the May 15 figure. \par \par \uc2  Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had fallen by $526 million in the week ended May 15, largely on account of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action to prop up the rupee, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  became necessary after it came under pressure on fears of foreign capital inflows slowing down after the United States and some other nations imposed economic sanctions against India for its nuclear tests on May 11 and May 13. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market, but supported the rupee through dollar sales by the State Bank of India. \par \par \uc2  "It is good that there has been an increase even if marginal," said an official at a state-run bank. "After the sharp fall in the previous week, even a slight increase should boost the sentiment." \par \par \uc2  The official said it was too early to predict the rupee's fortunes. \par \par \uc2  "A good deal depends on the budget and whether it revives foreign investor confidence," he said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Yashwant Sinha will present the federal budget for 1998/99 (April-March) on June 1 at 5 p.m. (1130 GMT). \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit a record closing low of 41.72/75 per dollar on Friday. \par \par \uc2  It has fallen some 4.5 percent from its pre-nuclear test levels on a combination of factors - fears over the impact of economic sanctions, a ratings outlook revision to negative from positive by Standard & Poor's and tit-for-tat nuclear tests by Pakistan last week. ((New Delhi Newsroom +91-11-301-2024 Fax +91-11-301-4043, delhi.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du61040pu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
