\par\par \b \uc2  =Indian Rupee/Budget -2: S&P Should Have Waited For Budget \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 1998\par 15:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Measures expected in the budget to attract foreign investments include a range of tax benefits for foreign investments in infrastructure projects and in Indian shares. \par \par \uc2  Some bankers said the government may also provide incentives to banks to raise interest rates on deposits held by expatriate Indians. \par \par \uc2  Some traders also said that S&P should have waited for the presentation of the government's budget before deciding on its change to the country's rating outlook. \par \par \uc2  "S&P's decision has come a little too early; it could have at least waited till the budget," said Sharukh Wadia, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Reserve Bank of India, which said on Saturday it will closely monitor the rupee following S&P's rating move late Friday, was "intriguingly" absent from the market Monday, one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Wadia said that the "RBI perhaps wants the rupee to depreciate slowly, given the pressure from exporters." \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, dealers said they expected the rupee to remain in the INR40.90 to INR41.50 levels against the dollar until the budget's presentation. \par \par \uc2  Wadia of Standard Chartered said he expected the rupee to fall by INR0.10 every day until the budget is released. "There isn't any panic from importers. They have covered nearly 50-70% of their dollar requirements," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said they expect the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market only if the rupee falls sharply and suddenly. "I see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the rupee drops suddenly to INR42," Abheek Barua strategist at SSKI Securities said. \par \par \uc2  Until then, the Reserve Bank is expected to support the rupee by selling dollars through the State Bank of India, the country's largest commercial bank. \par \par \uc2  In India's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the movement of the spot rupee is determined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  or by sales and purchases by the State Bank. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank owns 68% in State Bank and the market believes that the State Bank often operates in the market on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By S.Anuradha; (91 22) 288-4211;sanuradha@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires  25-05-98 \par \par \uc2  1305GMT \par \par \uc2  1164 1847 62506 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du5p00jsh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
